{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794253758950,"sessionID":"ses_e3e27e7a7ffejmOdEJ70WaOTRm","part":{"id":"prt_1c1dba1c1001gCmyhL9fbo1BlJ","messageID":"msg_1c1db8995001WYKT65evBiLw4X","sessionID":"ses_e3e27e7a7ffejmOdEJ70WaOTRm","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794253758950,"sessionID":"ses_e3e27e7a7ffejmOdEJ70WaOTRm","part":{"id":"prt_1c1dba1c5001pgkqrdGWCUGLXl","messageID":"msg_1c1db8995001WYKT65evBiLw4X","sessionID":"ses_e3e27e7a7ffejmOdEJ70WaOTRm","type":"text","text":"The notes app is built, but I haven't built the Docker image or tested the frontend in a browser.\n\n**What I ran:**\n- **API:** I ran the Flask test client against all the endpoints. That covered register, login, create, edit, delete, listing with tag, author, search and paging, and the tag counts. It also covered the 401, 403, 404 and validation errors.\n- **Server:** I ran it under gunicorn and checked `GET /api/health`, `/api/notes` and an unknown `/api/…` path, which returns a JSON 404. A `/notes/1` URL returns the frontend page.\n- **Frontend:** `npm run build` passes, and it includes a TypeScript check.\n\n**Choices not in the spec:**\n- **Tokens:** they are signed and expire after 7 days. The signing secret is generated on first start and saved in `data/secret.key`, so sign-ins survive a restart.\n- **Extra endpoint:** I added `GET /api/auth/me`, which returns the signed-in user. The frontend doesn't use it yet.\n- **Registration:** usernames are 3–32 characters and unique regardless of case. Passwords are 8–128 characters.\n- **Paging:** `page_size` defaults to 20 and is capped at 100. The frontend asks for 10 per page.\n- **Note limits:** titles are up to 200 characters and content up to 20,000. Notes can have up to 10 tags.\n- **Tags:** they are lowercased and de-duplicated. They can contain letters, digits, `-` and `_`.\n- **Plain text:** note content is rendered as text with line breaks kept, so HTML in a note is never interpreted.\n\nI also added `react-router-dom`, Tailwind, TypeScript and the React type packages to `frontend/package.json`. I added a `.gitignore`, and put `data/secret.key` in `.dockerignore` so it stays out of the image.\n\nThe backend is `backend/app.py`, and the frontend pages are in `frontend/src/`.","time":{"start":1794253758917,"end":1794253758922}}}
